***REMOVED*** Zug Zug backend — the three stores from ARCHITECTURE.md.
***REMOVED*** Copy to `server/.env` and fill in. Bun auto-loads .env from the cwd.

***REMOVED*** App state (OLTP): Postgres — drafts, audit, users, presence. Read/write.
***REMOVED*** Any Postgres works (Supabase, Neon, RDS, local). Example shapes:
***REMOVED***   postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname
***REMOVED***   postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

***REMOVED*** MotherDuck token — gives one connection both the warehouse (read-only scan)
***REMOVED*** and the Zug Zug canonical database (read/write dim_/map_). Get it at
***REMOVED*** https://app.motherduck.com → Settings → Access Tokens.
MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN=

***REMOVED*** The MotherDuck database that holds your existing warehouse source tables
***REMOVED*** (scanned read-only). Defaults to `analytics`. If your account is empty, run
***REMOVED*** `bun run bootstrap -- --seed` to provision a demo warehouse here.
WAREHOUSE_DB=analytics

***REMOVED*** Attach the MotherDuck warehouse (enables the discovery scan). Off by default —
***REMOVED*** Postgres-only canonical/draft/commit works without it. Flip to true once the
***REMOVED*** warehouse is wired (needs the motherduck extension + outbound network).
ATTACH_WAREHOUSE=false

***REMOVED*** The MotherDuck database Zug Zug owns and writes (dim_/map_). Created if absent.
ZUGZUG_DB=zugzug

***REMOVED*** Local DuckDB engine file (the "home" db that ATTACHes the two remotes).
***REMOVED*** ":memory:" is fine — all durable state lives in Postgres + MotherDuck.
DUCK_PATH=:memory:

PORT=8787

***REMOVED*** Google OAuth2 — create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
***REMOVED*** Authorized redirect URI must include: ORIGIN/api/auth/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

***REMOVED*** Domain restriction — only @this-domain.com emails may log in.
ALLOWED_DOMAIN=example.com

***REMOVED*** Public base URL of this app. Used to build the OAuth redirect_uri.
***REMOVED*** Dev: http://localhost:5173   Prod: https://yourapp.com
ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

***REMOVED*** Dev-only auth bypass — shows a "Dev mode" login button that skips Google OAuth.
***REMOVED*** NEVER set this in production.
DEV_BYPASS_AUTH=false

***REMOVED*** Optional: enables AI Triage suggestions (get a key at https://console.anthropic.com)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

***REMOVED*** Postgres pool sizing — defaults to 5 for the main pool.
***REMOVED*** Migrations run with their own max=1 connection.
PG_POOL_MAX=5
